  "result": "I want to write about borrowed light.\n\nThe moon doesn't make any light of its own. I love that fact. It's just a big, dusty rock hanging in the dark, and yet we write songs about its glow, we fall in love under it, we use it to find our way home. All that beauty is just reflected sun.\n\nAnd I think most beautiful things are like that.\n\nNone of us really generate our own light either. We reflect it.\n\nYou learned a joke from your dad that you still tell at parties. That joke is borrowed light. Your favorite word that you stole from a book you read when you were fourteen. The way you make coffee exactly the way your first roommate did. The kindness a stranger showed you on a bad Tuesday three years ago that you now show to other strangers without even thinking about it.\n\nWe are all just moons for each other.\n\nI think about this a lot \u2014 how the internet is often described as this loud, angry place, but really it's a giant sky full of moons. Someone has a thought at 2 a.m. in Seoul and someone else in Ohio feels a little less alone because of it. A photo of someone's messy desk, a three-sentence story, a weird fact about octopuses. Little reflections bouncing around forever.\n\nIf you really pay attention, you can see it in real life too. Look closely at anyone and you can see who they\u2019ve been orbiting.\n\nThe way my friend says \u201coh, cool cool cool\u201d exactly like her older sister. The way a barista draws a heart on the cup because a different barista once did it for her when she needed it. We\u2019re passing the same light back and forth, and somehow it doesn\u2019t get dimmer. It gets *brighter*.\n\nMaybe that\u2019s why small, ordinary days matter so much. Not every day has to be a supernova. Most days are just quiet reflections. You held the door. You texted her back. You made something, even if it was just a decent sandwich. And that tiny bit of light went out into the world and landed somewhere you\u2019ll never see.\n\nSo I guess if I can write about whatever I want, I want to write about that. That you \u2014 whoever you are, reading this \u2014 are probably glowing a little more than you think. Not with your own perfect, original, made-from-scratch light. But with all the borrowed light you\u2019ve collected and are now quietly carrying for someone else.\n\nWhat are you reflecting these days?\n\nAnd if you want \u2014 what should we shine a little light on together next?",
